<title>NEW ZEALAND: CRICKET-NZ CLINCHES FINAL VS ENGLAND, DRAWS SERIES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-NZ CLINCHES FINAL VS ENGLAND, DRAWS SERIES.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand won the fifth and final one-day cricket international against England at the Basin Reserve on Tuesday, bowling the tourists out for 200 after setting them 229 to win.</p>
<p>New Zealand and England draw the five-match one-day series 2-2 after the third game was tied in Napier last Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scores:</p>
<p>New Zealand 228 (N. Astle 94, A. Caddick 3-35).</p>
<p>England 200 (G. Thorpe 55, G. Larsen 2-31, N. Astle 2-26).</p>
